# Banning a site that's banned already. Smokegod (60) bans two sites and lifts both, so ROM's free list holds two
# recycled bans; then bans one site three times, each replacing the last, and lists the bans. ban_site freed the
# old ban and then followed its next pointer, now into the free list, comparing the site with the recycled bans'
# stale names (#20). That memory is still allocated, and free_mem overwrites a stale name's first bytes, so in
# practice nothing matched and nothing showed: this golden is the same before and after the fix, which stops the
# loop at the ban it replaces.
@connect god
Smokegod
smoke123
@return
@return
ban first.example
ban second.example
allow first.example
allow second.example
ban again.example
ban again.example newbies
ban again.example permit
ban
